 with input/output/cache tracking\n  - **Domain Alignment**: Good - standard token tracking patterns\n\n## 2. Store Layer (`internal/backend/store/`)\n\n### **Interface Design**\n- **File**: `internal/backend/store/store.go` (lines 183-192)\n- **Pattern**: Clean aggregate interface pattern\n- **Interfaces**: All repositories follow consistent naming conventions\n\n### **SQLite Implementation**\n- **File**: `internal/backend/store/sqlite.go`\n- **Pattern**: Concrete implementation wrapping `*sql.DB`\n- **Design**: Good separation with aggregate root (`SQLiteStore`)\n\n### **SQL Schema**\n- **File**: `internal/backend/store/migrations.go`\n- **Tables**:\n  - `machines` (lines 15-23)\n  - `projects` (lines 27-34)\n  - `sessions` (lines 37-56) - rich metadata tracking\n  - `issue_claims` (lines 59-72) - UNIQUE constraint on repo+issue\n  - `config` (lines 75-79) - key-value storage\n  - `proxies` (lines 82-88) - proxy registration\n- **Design**: Well-normalized with proper indexes\n\n### **Data Access Patterns**\n- **File**: `internal/backend/store/issue_store.go`\n- **Features**:\n  - Automatic record creation (lines 28-48)\n  - Optimistic locking for claims (line 92)\n  - Proper NULL handling with `sql.NullString`\n\n## 3. Service Layer (`internal/backend/service/`)\n\n### **Architecture Pattern**\n- **Pattern**: Thin service layer - mostly direct store delegation\n- **File**: `internal/backend/service/issue_service.go`\n\n### **Service Examples**\n1. **IssueService** (`internal/backend/service/issue_service.go`):\n   - Claims, status updates, releases\n   - All methods are simple store wrappers (lines 22-65)\n   \n2. **SessionService** (`internal/backend/service/session_service.go`):\n   - Registration, closing, listing\n   - Clean interface (lines 16-43)\n\n3. **ProxyService** (`internal/backend/service/proxy_service.go`):\n   - Simple proxy listing\n   - Minimal business logic\n\n### **Pain Points**:\n- **God Object Risk**: `StatusService` (lines 54-58 in `server.go`) depends on 5 stores\n- **Missing Abstractions**: Services don't hide implementation details\n\n## 4. API Layer (`internal/backend/api/`)\n\n### **Handler Pattern**\n- **File**: `internal/backend/api/router.go`\n- **Pattern**: Clean handler aggregation with `Handlers` struct (lines 11-21)\n\n### **Handler Structure**\n- Each handler takes service dependencies in constructor\n- Consistent error handling patterns\n- **File**: `internal/backend/api/issue_handler.go` (lines 16-23)\n\n### **Request/Response Types**\n- **File**: `internal/backend/api/request.go`\n- **Pattern**: Clear request DTOs with validation\n- **Design**: Good separation of concerns\n\n### **Routing**\n- RESTful conventions\n- Dynamic routing for session endpoints (lines 41-53)\n\n## 5. Proxy Path (`internal/proxy/`, `internal/sse/`, `internal/trace/`, `internal/usage/`)\n\n### **Proxy Architecture**\n- **File**: `internal/proxy/reverse.go`\n- **Key Components**:\n  - `ReverseProxy` struct (lines 23-41) with fallback support\n  - **Pattern**: Rich proxy with tracing capabilities\n\n### **SSE Handling**\n- **File**: `internal/sse/reassembler.go`\n- **Pattern**: Streaming response reconstruction\n- **Support**: Anthropic, OpenAI, Google Gemini\n\n### **Trace Recording**\n- **File**: `internal/trace/anthropic.go`\n- **Pattern**: JSONL format with structured records\n- **Design**: Comprehensive request/response tracking\n\n### **Usage Tracking**\n- **File**: `internal/usage/anthropic.go`\n- **Pattern**: Standardized usage metrics\n- **Alignment**: Good with industry standards\n\n### **End-to-End Flow**\n1. **Proxy Start** (`internal/proxy/reverse.go` lines 68-94)\n2. **Request Interception** with path whitelisting (`internal/proxy/paths.go`)\n3. **SSE Processing** for streaming responses\n4. **Trace Writing** to JSONL files\n5. **Backend Registration** via `trace-init` endpoint\n\n## 6. Entry Point (`cmd/claude-tap/main.go`)\n\n### **Command Pattern**\n- **Pattern**: Multi-mode CLI with clear subcommands\n- **Modes**:\n  - Proxy mode (default)\n  - Session management (push/pull/status)\n  - Backend server\n\n### **Dependency Injection**\n- **File**: `cmd/claude-tap/backend_cmd.go`\n- **Pattern**: Manual dependency wiring\n- **Design**: Good configuration handling\n\n## 7. Test Structure (`tests/`)\n\n### **Test Coverage**\n- **Total Test Files**: 26\n- **Critical Gap**: **ZERO unit tests** in domain, service, and store layers\n- **Existing Tests**:\n  - Integration tests (`tests/backend/`)\n  - E2E tests (`tests/e2e/`)\n  - API acceptance tests (`tests/backend/*_api_test.go`)\n\n### **Test Patterns**\n- **File**: `tests/backend/issue_api_test.go`\n- **Pattern**: Test environment setup with SQLite\n- **Design**: Good test isolation\n\n### **Coverage Gaps**:\n- ❌ Domain logic (no tests)\n- ❌ Service layer (no tests)\n- ❌ Store layer (no tests)\n- ❌ Component integration (minimal tests)\n\n## 8. Config (`internal/config/`)\n\n### **Configuration Hierarchy**\n- **Files**: \n  - `internal/config/claudeconfig.go` - Claude config integration\n  - `internal/config/profiles.go` - Profile management\n- **Pattern**: Multi-source configuration with precedence\n- **Design**: Flexible profile-based approach\n\n### **Key Features**:\n- Profile switching\n- Environment variable overrides\n- Claude Code integration\n\n## Key Architectural Patterns Used\n\n1. **Clean Architecture Domain-Store-Service-API layers**\n2. **Repository Pattern** with aggregate root\n3. **Dependency Injection** (manual wiring)\n4. **Command Query Separation** in store interfaces\n5. **Proxy Pattern** for API interception\n\n## Pain Points Identified\n\n1. **God Service Problem**:\n   - `StatusService` depends on 5 different stores\n   - Location: `internal/backend/server.go` lines 54-58\n\n2. **Missing Abstractions**:\n   - Services directly expose store implementation details\n   - No domain service interfaces\n\n3. **Tight Coupling**:\n   - Services know too much about store implementation\n   - No in