re layer (no tests)\n- ❌ Component integration (minimal tests)\n\n## 8. Config (`internal/config/`)\n\n### **Configuration Hierarchy**\n- **Files**: \n  - `internal/config/claudeconfig.go` - Claude config integration\n  - `internal/config/profiles.go` - Profile management\n- **Pattern**: Multi-source configuration with precedence\n- **Design**: Flexible profile-based approach\n\n### **Key Features**:\n- Profile switching\n- Environment variable overrides\n- Claude Code integration\n\n## Key Architectural Patterns Used\n\n1. **Clean Architecture Domain-Store-Service-API layers**\n2. **Repository Pattern** with aggregate root\n3. **Dependency Injection** (manual wiring)\n4. **Command Query Separation** in store interfaces\n5. **Proxy Pattern** for API interception\n\n## Pain Points Identified\n\n1. **God Service Problem**:\n   - `StatusService` depends on 5 different stores\n   - Location: `internal/backend/server.go` lines 54-58\n\n2. **Missing Abstractions**:\n   - Services directly expose store implementation details\n   - No domain service interfaces\n\n3. **Tight Coupling**:\n   - Services know too much about store implementation\n   - No interface segregation\n\n4. **Testability Issues**:\n   - No unit tests for business logic\n   - Mocking would be difficult due to tight coupling\n\n5. **Missing Error Abstractions**:\n   - Store errors are exposed directly to API layer\n\n## Domain Terminology Alignment\n\n**Strengths**:\n- Excellent alignment with GitHub workflow concepts\n- Clear machine/session/project terminology\n- Standard API terminology (claims, releases, status)\n\n**Minor Issues**:\n- Some backend-specific terms (e.g., \"claim\" might be confusing outside GitHub context)\n\n## What's Tested vs Not Tested\n\n### **Well Tested**:\n- ✅ API endpoints (26 integration tests)\n- ✅ End-to-end proxy functionality\n- ✅ Error handling at API level\n- ✅ Database operations (via integration tests)\n\n### **Not Tested**:\n- ❌ Business logic in services\n- ❌ Domain entity validation\n- ❌ Store error handling\n- ❌ Proxy edge cases\n- ❌ Configuration loading logic\n- ❌ Component isolation\n- ❌ Performance characteristics\n\n## Recommendations\n\n1. **Add unit tests** for domain entities and service logic\n2. **Extract service interfaces** to improve testability\n3. **Break up StatusService** into smaller, focused services\n4. **Add domain service layer** with business logic abstractions\n5. **Implement proper error handling** with domain-specific error types\n6. **Add component integration tests** to verify dependencies work together"}]}]}
